        <description>&lt;h3&gt;Corrected&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;**Managed model downloads work on Macs without a logged-in desktop session.** macOS reports zero &amp;quot;important usage&amp;quot; capacity when its space-accounting service is not running for the user, which made Spire refuse every managed download on headless machines despite ample free disk. Spire now falls back to the volume&amp;#x27;s plain available capacity, which excludes purgeable space and is therefore the more conservative figure. The 5 GiB reserve and the refusal on genuinely insufficient disk are unchanged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item>
